reagent-name-dh-sulfurdioxide = sulfur dioxide
reagent-desc-dh-sulfurdioxide = A choking, pungent gas from burning sulfur. A step towards sulfuric acid: oxidised over a catalyst into sulfur trioxide.
reagent-name-dh-sulfurtrioxide = sulfur trioxide
reagent-desc-dh-sulfurtrioxide = Reacts violently and hot with water to give sulfuric acid. Corrodes skin.
reagent-name-dh-nitricoxide = nitric oxide
reagent-desc-dh-nitricoxide = A colourless gas from oxidising ammonia. With oxygen it turns brown, becoming NO₂.
reagent-name-dh-nitrogendioxide = nitrogen dioxide
reagent-desc-dh-nitrogendioxide = The "fox tail": a brown poisonous gas that burns the lungs. With water it gives nitric acid.
reagent-name-dh-hydrogenchloride = hydrogen chloride
reagent-desc-dh-hydrogenchloride = A pungent gas made from salt and sulfuric acid with heat. In water it becomes hydrochloric acid.
reagent-name-dh-phosphoruspentoxide = phosphorus pentoxide
reagent-desc-dh-phosphoruspentoxide = A white powder from burning phosphorus. Greedily absorbs water to form phosphoric acid.
reagent-name-dh-nitricacid = nitric acid
reagent-desc-dh-nitricacid = A strong acid and oxidiser. Corrodes skin and metals.
reagent-name-dh-hydrochloricacid = hydrochloric acid
reagent-desc-dh-hydrochloricacid = Hydrogen chloride dissolved in water: a strong acid for synthesis.
reagent-name-dh-aceticacid = acetic acid
reagent-desc-dh-aceticacid = A weak organic acid at the base of many syntheses. Burns when concentrated.
reagent-name-dh-potassiumchloride = potassium chloride
reagent-desc-dh-potassiumchloride = A potassium salt: for Ringer's solution, and by electrolysis for potassium hydroxide.
reagent-name-dh-potassiumhydroxide = potassium hydroxide
reagent-desc-dh-potassiumhydroxide = Caustic potash: a strong alkali that corrodes skin.
reagent-name-dh-coppersulfate = copper sulfate
reagent-desc-dh-coppersulfate = Blue crystals that kill fungus and mould. Poisonous.
reagent-name-dh-ironsulfate = iron sulfate
reagent-desc-dh-ironsulfate = Greenish crystals: raw material for pigments and Prussian blue.
reagent-name-dh-ammoniumphosphate = ammonium phosphate
reagent-desc-dh-ammoniumphosphate = A fertiliser: nitrogen and phosphorus for plants.
reagent-name-dh-ironoxide = iron oxide
reagent-desc-dh-ironoxide = Rust: a pigment and the catalyst of the contact process.
reagent-name-dh-copperoxide = copper oxide
reagent-desc-dh-copperoxide = A black powder that gives copper sulfate with sulfuric acid.
reagent-name-dh-zincoxide = zinc oxide
reagent-desc-dh-zincoxide = A white powder: catalyst for methanol synthesis and the base of zinc ointment.
reagent-name-dh-silicondioxide = silicon dioxide
reagent-desc-dh-silicondioxide = Sand and quartz. Inert.
reagent-name-dh-methanol = methanol
reagent-desc-dh-methanol = Wood alcohol. Smells like ethanol, but it is poison that blinds and kills.
reagent-name-dh-formaldehyde = formaldehyde
reagent-desc-dh-formaldehyde = A pungent preservative for tissue and corpses. Poisonous.
reagent-name-dh-toluene = toluene
reagent-desc-dh-toluene = A solvent. The fumes stupefy and poison.
reagent-name-dh-glycerol = glycerol
reagent-desc-dh-glycerol = A sweet, thick liquid left over from soap-making; the base of ointments.
reagent-name-dh-urea = urea
reagent-desc-dh-urea = A nitrogen fertiliser.

dh-chemistry-toxic-fumes = A pungent cloud rises from the mixture!
dh-entity-effect-guidebook-toxic-fumes = Part of the product escapes as a poisonous cloud ({$reagent})
